# Fault (coordinator): a plan whose amount reads flows of another plan was refused RUN-CYCLE.  E §4.1: plans read
# other plans through flows(m[keys], span), and the instance graph is acyclic; flows of a plan isn't a running read
# (E §3.1 step 7), so echo_pay declares no reads.  rent books amt = 10.00 PLN (a bare literal in a row takes its
# target's type, L §7.1) on the 1st of each month; echo_pay pays flows(rent, m) = 10.00 PLN the next day, six months
# in the run: 60.00 PLN.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-15
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..
index month = month 2026-01..2026-06
input amt: money PLN
move rent[m in month]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt
move echo_pay[m in month]: transfers
  on add_days(start_of(m), 1)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount flows(rent, m)
source s "x"
version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-31
  amt = 10
  opening[konto] = 0 at 2026-01-01 start
ask q: flows(echo_pay, 2026) law cut
=== expect
q: 60.00 PLN
...
